From: ms178 <ms178@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] elfutils: recognise SFrame, and drop a stray C comment
 from an AWK script

This patch folds together two independent fixes:

  A. SFrame support (SHT_GNU_SFRAME / PT_GNU_SFRAME) - fixes three
     testsuite failures.
  B. The previously separate remove-comment.patch - a stray C-style
     comment in config/known-dwarf.awk.

=====================================================================
A. SFrame support
=====================================================================

Fixes three testsuite failures seen when elfutils is built against a
toolchain whose glibc CRT files carry an .sframe section:

    FAIL: run-elflint-self.sh
    FAIL: run-reverse-sections-self.sh
    FAIL: run-strip-strmerge.sh

all of which report

    program header entry 12: unknown program header entry type 0x6474e554
    section [18] '.sframe' has unsupported type 1879048180

ROOT CAUSE

SFrame is the stack-trace format introduced in binutils 2.41 and enabled
by default in recent distribution toolchains.  The linker synthesises a
.sframe output section of type SHT_GNU_SFRAME (0x6ffffff4) and a
covering PT_GNU_SFRAME (0x6474e554) program header whenever any input
object contributes SFrame data - on Arch that is glibc's crt1.o, so
*every* dynamically linked executable gets one.

elfutils 0.195 knows PT_GNU_SFRAME as a constant in libelf/elf.h but
handles it nowhere, and does not define SHT_GNU_SFRAME at all.  So:

  - eblsegmenttypename.c falls through to the "LOOS+%d" catch-all, and
    elflint's list of accepted OS-specific segment types does not
    include PT_GNU_SFRAME, so it errors out;
  - eblsectiontypename.c returns NULL for 0x6ffffff4, which is exactly
    the condition elflint uses to decide a section type is unsupported.

The three failing tests are the "self" tests: they run elflint over
elfutils' own freshly linked binaries, which is why they are the ones
that trip.  Nothing is actually wrong with the binaries.

This is not an optimizer or a codegen problem.  The .sframe section is
present at -O0 exactly as at -O3, since it comes from the CRT files at
link time; it is independent of CFLAGS entirely.

THE FIX

  1. libelf/elf.h
     Define SHT_GNU_SFRAME 0x6ffffff4, in its correct slot immediately
     below SHT_GNU_ATTRIBUTES.

  2. libebl/eblsectiontypename.c
     Return "GNU_SFRAME" for it, alongside the other GNU additions.

  3. libebl/eblsegmenttypename.c
     Return "GNU_SFRAME" for PT_GNU_SFRAME, alongside PT_GNU_PROPERTY.

     Both names match what binutils readelf prints, so eu-readelf and
     readelf now agree.

  4. src/elflint.c
     Accept PT_GNU_SFRAME in the program-header type check and
     SHT_GNU_SFRAME in the section-header type check, and add .sframe to
     the special_sections table as SHT_GNU_SFRAME with exactly SHF_ALLOC.

     The last part is deliberate: rather than merely tolerating the
     section, elflint now *validates* it, and will report a .sframe that
     has the wrong type or unexpected flags.  This matches how every
     other known special section is handled and keeps elflint useful.

VALIDATION

  make check before:  251 pass, 3 fail   (the three listed above)
  make check after:   251 pass, 0 fail, exit status 0

  eu-readelf -S now prints "GNU_SFRAME" instead of "LOOS+0xffffff4",
  and eu-readelf -l prints "GNU_SFRAME" for the segment, both matching
  binutils readelf.

  Re-verified with a substantially more aggressive flag set than the
  reporter's (adding -floop-nest-optimize -fgraphite-identity -fipa-pta
  -fmodulo-sched -funroll-loops -flive-range-shrinkage): still
  251 pass / 0 fail, confirming the failures were never
  optimization-dependent.

=====================================================================
B. config/known-dwarf.awk: stray C comment
=====================================================================

  if (set ~ /SECT_.+/) set = "SECT"; /* */

AWK has no /* */ comment syntax.  gawk parses "/* */" here as a regular
expression literal used in a boolean context, which is harmless in
practice but is certainly not what was meant, and some awk
implementations reject it outright.  Removed.

This was previously carried as a separate remove-comment.patch; it is
folded in here so the package needs only one patch file.
diff -urN elf-pristine/config/known-dwarf.awk elfutils/config/known-dwarf.awk
--- a/config/known-dwarf.awk	2026-04-15 22:29:52.000000000 +0000
+++ b/config/known-dwarf.awk	2026-08-04 00:53:11.165408223 +0000
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
   sub(/_[^[:upper:]_].*$/, "", set);
   if (set ~ /LANG_.+/) set = "LANG";
   if (set ~ /LNAME_.+/) set = "LNAME";
-  if (set ~ /SECT_.+/) set = "SECT"; /* */
+  if (set ~ /SECT_.+/) set = "SECT";
 }
 
 $1 ~ /DW([_A-Z]+)_([^ ]+)/ {
diff -urN elf-pristine/libebl/eblsectiontypename.c elfutils/libebl/eblsectiontypename.c
--- a/libebl/eblsectiontypename.c	2026-04-15 22:29:52.000000000 +0000
+++ b/libebl/eblsectiontypename.c	2026-08-04 00:27:35.509408223 +0000
@@ -101,6 +101,9 @@
 	  case SHT_GNU_ATTRIBUTES:
 	    res = "GNU_ATTRIBUTES";
 	    break;
+	  case SHT_GNU_SFRAME:
+	    res = "GNU_SFRAME";
+	    break;
 
 	/* A few LLVM additions.  */
 
diff -urN elf-pristine/libebl/eblsegmenttypename.c elfutils/libebl/eblsegmenttypename.c
--- a/libebl/eblsegmenttypename.c	2026-04-15 22:29:52.000000000 +0000
+++ b/libebl/eblsegmenttypename.c	2026-08-04 00:27:35.509408223 +0000
@@ -67,6 +67,8 @@
 	res = "GNU_RELRO";
       else if (segment == PT_GNU_PROPERTY)
 	res = "GNU_PROPERTY";
+      else if (segment == PT_GNU_SFRAME)
+	res = "GNU_SFRAME";
       else if (segment == PT_SUNWBSS)
 	res = "SUNWBSS";
       else if (segment == PT_SUNWSTACK)
diff -urN elf-pristine/libelf/elf.h elfutils/libelf/elf.h
--- a/libelf/elf.h	2026-04-15 22:29:52.000000000 +0000
+++ b/libelf/elf.h	2026-08-04 00:27:35.505408223 +0000
@@ -447,6 +447,7 @@
 #define SHT_RELR	  19            /* RELR relative relocations */
 #define	SHT_NUM		  20		/* Number of defined types.  */
 #define SHT_LOOS	  0x60000000	/* Start OS-specific.  */
+#define SHT_GNU_SFRAME	  0x6ffffff4	/* SFrame stack trace section.  */
 #define SHT_GNU_ATTRIBUTES 0x6ffffff5	/* Object attributes.  */
 #define SHT_GNU_HASH	  0x6ffffff6	/* GNU-style hash table.  */
 #define SHT_GNU_LIBLIST	  0x6ffffff7	/* Prelink library list */
diff -urN elf-pristine/src/elflint.c elfutils/src/elflint.c
--- a/src/elflint.c	2026-04-15 22:29:52.000000000 +0000
+++ b/src/elflint.c	2026-08-04 00:28:14.301408223 +0000
@@ -3726,6 +3726,7 @@
     { ".gnu.version_d", 15, SHT_GNU_verdef, exact, SHF_ALLOC, 0 },
     { ".gnu.version_r", 15, SHT_GNU_verneed, exact, SHF_ALLOC, 0 },
     { ".gnu.attributes", 16, SHT_GNU_ATTRIBUTES, exact, 0, 0 },
+    { ".sframe", 8, SHT_GNU_SFRAME, exact, SHF_ALLOC, 0 },
   };
 #define nspecial_sections \
   (sizeof (special_sections) / sizeof (special_sections[0]))
@@ -3977,6 +3978,7 @@
 
       if (shdr->sh_type >= SHT_NUM
 	  && shdr->sh_type != SHT_GNU_ATTRIBUTES
+	  && shdr->sh_type != SHT_GNU_SFRAME
 	  && shdr->sh_type != SHT_GNU_LIBLIST
 	  && shdr->sh_type != SHT_CHECKSUM
 	  && shdr->sh_type != SHT_GNU_verdef
@@ -4597,6 +4599,7 @@
       if (phdr->p_type >= PT_NUM && phdr->p_type != PT_GNU_EH_FRAME
 	  && phdr->p_type != PT_GNU_STACK && phdr->p_type != PT_GNU_RELRO
 	  && phdr->p_type != PT_GNU_PROPERTY
+	  && phdr->p_type != PT_GNU_SFRAME
 	  /* Check for a known machine-specific type.  */
 	  && ebl_segment_type_name (ebl, phdr->p_type, NULL, 0) == NULL)
 	ERROR (_("\
